+# MOTION — short, reduced-motion-aware UI feedback
+
+Adds 180ms HUD number ticks, level/loot/mint confirmation cues and Forge reveal; panel entry is 140ms. Hover/press feedback is 100ms. All final states are immediate under reduced motion. Existing mint, API, wallet and reward logic stays authoritative; the layer only observes values.
+
+Fixed numeric columns and a stable level badge prevent shifts across 12→240,000 Fish and level9→10. Recent-loot labels occupy a fixed row, and left-aligned tabular text prevents glyph-origin shifts. The browser contract requires CLS exactly0 including recent-input shifts. Compact Forge confirmation disables browser scroll anchoring so its expanded actions remain visible.
+
+Builder: typecheck, lint, build and92 focused motion/HUD/shell/contrast cases passed. All13 regression browser cases passed after fixing the real layout shifts and compact scroll regression; a subsequent9-case run also covers level9→10 and bounded sample cards. Initial failures and two CLS source probes remain in reports/ui/logs/motion-builder. No assertion or threshold was weakened. The prior Forge event-count test now tracks the new animation name while preserving exact start/end/replay counts.
+
+The isolated fixture uses real HUD/RecentLoot and cue components, labelled sample mint/relic state, and no persistence/network writes. It is not a funded mint. Performance: four4-second RAF samples at1280×720/1600×900,normal/reduced, average60.001–60.002fps,p9516.7ms,CLS0,zero console errors/writes. No screenshots occur in the timing window. The inherited real-stage effects audit also passes10/10checks at each size; its screenshot-heavy software-GL measurement is a separate relative diagnostic (about60fps). See performance/fps.json and screenshots/ui/motion-effects-* evidence. Fresh A/B gates are pending. Release remains subject to the shared backend health hold.
+
+Fresh A at7d0427c correctly failed six landing pixel-grid assertions (fractional0.000009–0.000031px remainder) while the panel translated. All123other changed cases passed; no full matrix ran. Changed panel entry to a140ms opacity transition so existing pixel geometry remains exact. The unchanged journey/motion specs then passed18/18 repeated cases. Failure logs remain motion-a; the corrected fresh gate will use a new exact head.
+
+The corrected opacity version was remeasured without other UI browser jobs: all4samples60.001–60.002fps,p9516.7ms,CLS0; inheritedeffects10/10atbothsizes again passed. New evidence is performance-opacity/fps.json and screenshots/ui/motion-effects-opacity-*. Prior evidence remains preserved.
+
+Final visual review found the representable maximum Fish amount wrapping outside its36px HUD chip, despite the earlier command gate. The numeric column now reserves11ch for Fish; a new vertical-containment assertion in the existing state matrix prevents recurrence. The unchanged earlier tests plus the stronger matrix and motion contract pass57/57. Both maximum-value captures were visually checked.
+
+Final corrected measurement: four isolated RAF samples59.75–60.00fps,p95<=16.8ms,CLS0,zero console errors/writes. Inherited screenshot-heavy stage diagnostics pass10/10 at each size (59.8fps at1280;58.2fps at1600 with17ms p95 and no >250ms stalls). Those relative stage diagnostics are distinct from the isolated nominal60fps UI target. Final evidence: performance-final/ and screenshots/ui/motion-effects-final-*. Fresh A/B will run on the corrected frozen head; no accepted grade is claimed for57ef003.
+
+Real first-earn review also exposed an inherited Recent finds heading at2.296:1 contrast: the legacy root-without-theme fallback put brown text on the night card. Scoped that heading to the existing accent token. Both real30-second journeys reproduced the failure without weakening the4.5:1 threshold; the FIRSTPLAY card retains the rendered contrast regression. Interrupted760c92e freshA during its changed-spec phase to include this repair before grading; no full matrix ran on that head. The isolated performance fixture has no gains heading, so this selector does not change its measured geometry or animation.
+
+Full fresh A on0df4347 passed375/377 but correctly failed two1280late-chapter HUD geometry cases: fixed columns overran the Cat status region by13.90625px when Chapter5/Round10/10kills was shown. CleanB otherwise passed its changed checks,20/20resize and18-view audit; neither candidate receives an accepted grade. Reduced the Yarn numeric reservation to7ch (the full999,999cap) and used the existing4px column gap at1200–1399px. Fish keeps11ch, the XP track keeps160px, and no text or assertion is hidden or reduced. The original HUD geometry test now includes measured chip bounds in failure messages and is part of every subsequent changed-spec gate. Failed full-suite and red-reproducer logs are retained.
+
+The corrected HUD builder passes32/32, including the unchanged four baseline reference PNGs, all late-chapter/fallback/offline/error HUD checks, maximum-balance containment and normal/reduced CLS0. Four additional late-chapter captures pass4/4. Release performance is freshly measured in performance-release/fps.json: four samples60.0025fps,p95<=16.8ms,CLS0,no errors/writes. Both full-stage diagnostics pass10/10,60.0fps,p9517ms,no>250msstalls; recordings are screenshots/ui/motion-effects-release-*. Final frozen-head freshA/B checks remain required before grading or pushing.
+
+A pinned axe-core 4.10.3 scan rejected the next release candidate: the sample Home tab referenced no panel, the stage canvas label had no image role, and the empty bag slot scroller had no keyboard focus target. Added the fixture panel association, an image role, and a named focusable bag region. The unchanged catalog keyboard regression also exposed an overlapping native End/Home scroll animation; the shared tab host now handles boundary keys instantly only when a focused scroll container receives them, preserving control and tab keys. A new two-size regression enters the empty bag region with Tab and checks End/Home. No dependency or gameplay file changed. The first focused builder passed35/36; its lone failure used the old motion-parent screenshot preparation before the already-reviewed two-paint preparation from PREVIEWS. That diagnostic preparation is now shared upstream, keeping all four baseline PNGs and the exact byte assertion unchanged. Fresh review is required.
+
+Corrected focused builder: typecheck and36/36 repeated browser checks PASS, including both keyboard regions, all four unchanged baseline PNGs, and normal/reduced CLS0. The previous35/36 failure is retained. The final frozen-head A/B gate includes pinned axe scans as a blocking check.
+
+Accepted fresh review at4b0e69a: A95/B95 self-graded (fresh pass). All16A/14B commands pass; unchanged theme contrast test,195changed cases per size per reviewer,379full cases per size once on exact head,20/20resize per reviewer,18strict views and22axe scans with zero confirmed violations. Native maximum-balance/late-chapter captures reviewed. Axe incompletes remain disclosed. Evidence and grades are on ai/codex-ui-ledger. Release parked under SYSTEM health hold.
